@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-powers`

-- ca-tests-powers.l4
--
-- The sections that give or imply a power: 23(4), 24, 31 and 34.1.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act, before the module was run.
-- TRUE where the text names the power or states the condition and it is met; FALSE where a subsection says in terms that nothing
-- authorizes a thing; `#ASSERT REFUSED` for a case the text does not address.

§ `Section 23(4): remuneration`

-- "Where a person is appointed to an office, the appointing authority may fix, vary or terminate that person’s remuneration."
#ASSERT `the appointing authority of an office may, as to the remuneration of the person appointed to it,` `fix it`
#ASSERT `the appointing authority of an office may, as to the remuneration of the person appointed to it,` `vary it`
#ASSERT `the appointing authority of an office may, as to the remuneration of the person appointed to it,` `terminate it`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the appointing authority of an office may, as to the remuneration of the person appointed to it,` `something else`)

§ `Section 24: powers that words imply`

-- (1) Words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to terminate the appointment or
-- remove or suspend the officer; to re-appoint or reinstate the officer; and to appoint another person in the stead of, or to act in the
-- stead of, the officer.
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `terminate the appointment`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `remove the public officer`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `suspend the public officer`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `re-appoint the public officer`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `reinstate the public officer`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `appoint another person in the stead of the public officer`
#ASSERT `words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `appoint another person to act in the stead of the public officer`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` `some other power`)
-- (2) Words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include (a) a minister acting for that minister or, if the
-- office is vacant, a minister designated by or under an order in council; (b) the successors; (c) the deputy; (d) a person appointed to serve
-- in the department or ministry of state in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing.
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `a minister acting for that minister`
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `if the office is vacant, a minister designated to act in the office by or under the authority of an order in council`
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `a successor of that minister in the office`
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `the deputy of that minister, or of the successors`
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `a person appointed to serve, in the department or ministry of state over which the minister presides, in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `someone else`)
-- (3) "Nothing in paragraph (2)(c) or (d) shall be construed as authorizing the exercise of any authority conferred on a minister to make a
-- regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act."
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph 24(2)(c) or (d) authorizes the exercise of an authority conferred on a minister, where` TRUE)
#ASSERT `paragraph 24(2)(c) or (d) authorizes the exercise of an authority conferred on a minister, where` FALSE
-- (4) Words directing or empowering any public officer other than a minister to do an act or thing, or applying to the officer by name of
-- office, include the officer’s successors in the office and the officer’s or their deputy.
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a public officer other than a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `a successor of the public officer in the office`
#ASSERT `words directing or empowering a public officer other than a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `the deputy of the public officer, or of the successors`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words directing or empowering a public officer other than a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` `someone else`)
-- (5) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed on the holder of an office, it may be exercised, and must be performed, by the person for
-- the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office.
#ASSERT `a power conferred on the holder of an office may be exercised, and a duty imposed on the holder shall be performed, by a person who is` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power conferred on the holder of an office may be exercised, and a duty imposed on the holder shall be performed, by a person who is` FALSE)

§ `Section 31: miscellaneous rules about powers`

-- (1) "Where anything is required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, provincial court judge, justice of the peace or any
-- functionary or officer, it shall be done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done."
#ASSERT `a thing required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, justice of the peace, functionary or officer is done as section 31(1) requires, where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, justice of the peace, functionary or officer is done as section 31(1) requires, where` FALSE)
-- (2) "Where power is given to a person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of any act or thing, all such powers as are
-- necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are deemed to be also given."
#ASSERT `a power is deemed also given to a person, officer or functionary who is given power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, where` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power is deemed also given to a person, officer or functionary who is given power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, where` FALSE)
-- (3) "Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as
-- occasion requires."
#ASSERT `from time to time, as occasion requires, it is open to exercise or perform` `a power conferred` `where` TRUE
#ASSERT `from time to time, as occasion requires, it is open to exercise or perform` `a duty imposed` `where` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`from time to time, as occasion requires, it is open to exercise or perform` `a power conferred` `where` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`from time to time, as occasion requires, it is open to exercise or perform` `a duty imposed` `where` FALSE)
-- (4) "Where a power is conferred to make regulations, the power shall be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and
-- subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and make others."
#ASSERT `a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` `repeal the regulations`
#ASSERT `a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` `amend the regulations`
#ASSERT `a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` `vary the regulations`
#ASSERT `a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` `make other regulations`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` `something else`)
#ASSERT `the included power is the one section 31(4) describes where` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the included power is the one section 31(4) describes where` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the included power is the one section 31(4) describes where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the included power is the one section 31(4) describes where` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 34.1: entering a dwelling-house to arrest`

-- "Any person who may issue a warrant to arrest or apprehend a person under any Act of Parliament, other than the Criminal Code, has the same
-- powers ... (a) to authorize the entry into a dwelling-house described in the warrant ..., if the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by
-- information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person is or will be present in the dwelling-house."
#ASSERT `the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house described in it where` TRUE `and` TRUE `that` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house described in it where` TRUE `and` FALSE `that` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house described in it where` TRUE `and` TRUE `that` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house described in it where` FALSE `and` TRUE `that` TRUE)
-- (b) "to authorize the entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement if the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met."
#ASSERT `the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement where` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement where` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
